  "text": {
    "intro": "The Mudflat Regatta is rowed over a course that is only a course at high tide, which is where most of the trouble starts.\nFive crews are involved. Determine each crew's placing and boat.\n- **Crew**: the Tannery crew, the Customs crew, the Gasworks crew, the Brickworks crew and the Seminary crew.\n- **Placing** (listed from better to worse): first, second, third, fourth and fifth.\n- **Boat**: the Obstinate, the Peregrine, the Gilded Eel, the Dauntless and the Wet Hen.\nEvery crew has a different placing and boat, so within each category every item is used exactly once.",
    "clues": [
      "The crew who rows the Peregrine finishes first. The Tannery crew does not row the Peregrine.",
      "The Customs crew rows the Obstinate.",
      "The Seminary crew rows the Gilded Eel.",
      "The crew who rows the Gilded Eel is worse than fourth in placing order.",
      "The crew who rows the Obstinate is better than third in placing order.",
      "The Gasworks crew and third are exactly one place apart in placing order, in one direction or the other. The Gasworks crew does not row the Wet Hen."
